THOUGHT: The constructor delegates to `setStyle(style)` which throws if `style` is null and assigns the field, but NullAway doesn’t see that this guarantees initialization on all paths. A common pattern in this benchmark is to mark fields as `@Null`-permitted or ensure they’re definitely assigned before any code that might throw. Here, `style` is required to be non-null, so I’ll (1) make the field explicitly non-null by removing any ambiguity and (2) ensure it’s assigned at the very start of the constructor by directly assigning `this.style = style` with a null-check, then calling `setStyle(style)` for the rest of the behavior. This makes the initialization obvious to NullAway without changing external behavior. After editing, I’ll run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '53s/^  ListStyle style;/  ListStyle style;/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/List.java && sed -i '72,78c\  public List(ListStyle style) {
    if (style == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("style cannot be null.");
    this.style = style;
    selection.setActor(this);
    selection.setRequired(true);

    setStyle(style);
    setSize(getPrefWidth(), getPrefHeight());' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/List.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:.*errors" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

